---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Athan, at home">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> OPEN SOURCE. STANDALONE. YOURS.</p><h1>
        A familiar call.<br />A place in your day.
      </h1><p class="lede">
        Bring the Athan into your home with a small, standalone speaker. Prayer times calculated
        locally. Recordings stored on your device.
      </p><div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/install/">Set up OpenAthan <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a
          class="text-link"
          href="/guides/setup/">Explore the setup guide</a
        >
      </div><p class="release-note">
        Early development · Public installation is not available yet.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-art" aria-label="A decorative arch with sound waves">
      <div class="art-orbit orbit-one"></div><div class="art-orbit orbit-two"></div><div
        class="arch-art"
      >
        <svg viewBox="0 0 180 110" aria-hidden="true"
          ><path
            d="M15 55h14m12-13v26m13-40v54m13-54v54m13-68v82m13-59v36m13-45v54m13-67v80m13-67v54m13-40v26m13-20v14"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="4"
            stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg
        >
      </div><span class="art-caption">A moment to pause.</span><span
        class="art-number"
        aria-hidden="true">05 / EVERY DAY</span
      >
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="principles wrap" aria-label="What makes OpenAthan different">
    <article>
      <span class="number">01</span><h2>At home, on its own.</h2><p>
        Your speaker keeps its settings and plays stored recordings without this website or Home
        Assistant.
      </p>
    </article><article>
      <span class="number">02</span><h2>Your prayer settings.</h2><p>
        Choose your location, calculation method, prayer offsets and volume from the device’s local
        page.
      </p>
    </article><article>
      <span class="number">03</span><h2>Open by design.</h2><p>
        Built in the open, with documented hardware and software you can inspect and contribute to.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section class="home-guide wrap">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">THE REFERENCE BUILD</p><h2>Two modules.<br />One place to start.</h2><p>
        The reference hardware pairs an M5Stack AtomS3R C126 with the Pyramid A167 speaker base. No
        soldering or separate home server is needed.
      </p>
    </div><a class="guide-card" href="/guides/setup/"
      ><span class="eyebrow">GETTING STARTED</span><strong>From your desk<br />to your home.</strong
      ><span>Hardware, cables and the setup steps <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a
    >
  </section>
</Layout>
